# CVEs Trivy may skip in the image scan (build-image-stage.yml, build-image-prod.yml).
# Only for a vulnerability with no fixed package available yet. One ID per line,
# with a comment: package, fixed version, and when to remove the line.
# The image refreshes apk packages daily (APK_REFRESH), so a fixed package is
# picked up on the next day's build.

# CVE-2026-102633: libexpat 2.8.5-r0; the fix (2.9.0-r0) is only in Alpine edge and not yet backported to Alpine 3.24.
# Only git depends on libexpat in the image (PHP XML uses libxml2), so exposure is minimal.
# Track: https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/packages?name=libexpat&branch=v3.24
# Remove once Alpine 3.24 ships libexpat >= 2.9.0-r0.
CVE-2026-102633
